{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{
  "protocol": "legalmath.search.v1",
  "task": "GENERATE",
  "source_key": "assurance.905bdc6bde75569bab1f4310",
  "proposal_status": "Source-grounded interpretation for review, not an approval or determination of legal correctness.",
  "selected_control": {
    "name": "Paragraph 10 gift restriction for a selected promotional offer",
    "question": "Does the selected offer contain an offered gift component, other than a discount of fees or charges, used by a distributor to promote a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client?",
    "boundary": "This control addresses the gift restriction described in paragraph 10. It does not determine whole-firm compliance, section 103 liability, licence possession, advertising compliance or redemption-right compliance."
  },
  "interpretations": [
    {
      "id": "component_specific_gift_restriction",
      "reading": "A distributor should not offer a gift to a client when promoting either a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product, including gifts linked to certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses. A discount of fees or charges is excepted. Guaranteed returns and other incentives require classification: the packet says they may be considered gifts, rather than declaring that every such incentive is a gift. For a combined offer, the discount exception attaches to the component that qualifies as a discount; its presence does not itself exempt a separate gift component.",
      "source_anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
          "quote": "distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
          "quote": "If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u12.2646",
          "quote": "as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors."
        }
      ],
      "substantive_difference": "This reading can capture a campaign promoting a fund category even without a named individual fund. It does not automatically classify every additional return as a gift, and it does not allow a fee discount to exempt a separate gift in the same offer. A finding that an arrangement is not a structured product does not dispose of the gift question.",
      "derivation_boundary": "The component-specific treatment follows from the exception modifying gifts that are discounts of fees or charges. The source does not expressly prescribe how to separate, value or allocate components of a combined offer.",
      "strongest_uncertainty": "The packet supplies neither a complete definition of gift nor a test for deciding when a rebate, top-up or economically combined benefit is a discount of fees or charges. Those classifications may determine the result and cannot be inferred from marketing labels alone.",
      "formalization": {
        "notation": "parenthesized_prefix",
        "evaluation_unit": "One selected offer by one selected actor to a client, with all separately identifiable benefit components assessed.",
        "scope": "(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client product_or_type_link)",
        "result_type": "Boolean",
        "result": "(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client product_or_type_link has_offered_non_discount_gift_component)",
        "statement": "[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] True means that the selected offer falls within the distributor, client and promotional-link scope and contains at least one offered gift component that does not qualify as a discount of fees or charges, so it is caught by the quoted should-not-offer restriction. False means that at least one of those conditions is established to be absent; it does not establish compliance with other requirements. The marker denotes this selected restriction and does not convert its wording into a statutory offence.",
        "unknown_handling": "No fact values are supplied. Unknown inputs remain unknown; an unresolved classification must not be entered as false. A result is determinate only when known inputs logically establish it.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "name": "actor_is_distributor",
            "type": "Boolean",
            "definition": "Whether the selected actor is an intermediary who distributes SFC-authorised funds, using the circular's definition of distributor.",
            "units": "Boolean; no physical or monetary units",
            "source_refs": [
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u0.2",
                "quote": "Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)"
              }
            ],
            "requires_professional_judgment": true,
            "judgment_reason": "Applying the described actor category to the selected entity and its activities requires a scope assessment."
          },
          {
            "name": "promotion_to_client",
            "type": "Boolean",
            "definition": "Whether the selected offer is made in promotional activity directed to a client. This does not require an invitation to the Hong Kong public.",
            "units": "Boolean; no physical or monetary units",
            "source_refs": [
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
                "quote": "in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client."
              }
            ],
            "requires_professional_judgment": true,
            "judgment_reason": "The relationship between the communication, offer and client must be assessed."
          },
          {
            "name": "product_or_type_link",
            "type": "Boolean",
            "definition": "Whether the selected offer promotes a specific investment product or is linked to a particular type of investment product, including certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses.",
            "units": "Boolean; no physical or monetary units",
            "source_refs": [
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
                "quote": "a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product"
              },
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
                "quote": "such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses"
              }
            ],
            "requires_professional_judgment": true,
            "judgment_reason": "The packet gives examples but no exhaustive test for promotional linkage or product-type boundaries."
          },
          {
            "name": "has_offered_non_discount_gift_component",
            "type": "Boolean",
            "definition": "Whether at least one component actually offered within the selected offer is classified as a gift and is not itself a discount of fees or charges. Assess separate components individually: a discount component does not erase a distinct non-discount gift. Guaranteed returns or other incentives are not automatically classified as gifts. False requires sufficient evidence that no offered component meets both conditions.",
            "units": "Boolean; no physical or monetary units",
            "source_refs": [
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
                "quote": "any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges)"
              },
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u12.2646",
                "quote": "such returns or other incentives"
              },
              {
                "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u12.2646",
                "quote": "may be considered a gift"
              }
            ],
            "requires_professional_judgment": true,
            "judgment_reason": "Supplying this fact requires identifying all offered components and resolving gift and discount classifications. The formula does not perform those classifications."
          }
        ],
        "representational_limit": "The expression represents the selected restriction conditional on supplied classifications. It does not formalize a general legal definition of gift, component allocation or the contents of missing referenced materials."
      }
    }
  ],
  "alternative_reading_assessment": {
    "conclusion": "One supported reading is proposed. The packet supports unresolved classification questions more strongly than a second materially different rule.",
    "unsupported_alternatives": [
      "Limiting the restriction to individually named products would omit the express coverage of particular product types.",
      "Exempting an entire combined offer whenever it includes a fee discount would extend the exception beyond its stated attachment.",
      "Treating all guaranteed returns as gifts would remove the qualification may be considered.",
      "Treating the gift restriction as applicable only after a finding that an arrangement is not a structured product would turn Even where into an exclusive condition."
    ],
    "unresolved_questions": [
      "When does a cash rebate or top-up qualify substantively as a discount of fees or charges?",
      "How should an economically inseparable combined benefit be divided or classified?",
      "What evidence establishes a sufficient link between a broad promotional campaign and a particular product type?",
      "How does the quoted Code provision apply beyond the SFC-authorised-fund distributor context used by this circular?",
      "What do the referenced FAQ and applicable Code version add to these classifications?"
    ]
  },
  "dimensions": {
    "scope": {
      "interpretation": "The circular identifies distributors as intermediaries distributing SFC-authorised funds. The quoted gift provision covers promotion to a client of a specific product or a particular product type. Its scope is distinct from section 103's person issuing an invitation to the Hong Kong public.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u0.2",
          "quote": "Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u9.1940",
          "quote": "for a person to issue an advertisement, invitation or document"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
          "quote": "to a client"
        }
      ]
    },
    "definitions": {
      "interpretation": "Guaranteed returns are described as comprising actual fund return and a distributor top-up. That economic description does not itself settle structured-product or gift classification. Gift and discount lack complete definitions in the packet.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u7.1360",
          "quote": "a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u8.1651",
          "quote": "may constitute a \"structured product\" under the SFO"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u12.2646",
          "quote": "may be considered a gift"
        }
      ]
    },
    "exceptions": {
      "interpretation": "The fee-or-charge discount exception attaches to the gift restriction. SFC authorisation or an exemption attaches separately to the section 103 offence description. Neither exception is stated to excuse the other requirement.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
          "quote": "(other than a discount of fees or charges)"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u9.1940",
          "quote": "unless the SFC has authorised the issue or an exemption applies."
        }
      ]
    },
    "modality": {
      "interpretation": "The selected restriction uses should not. The gift classification uses may. Section 103 is separately described as an offence, while other passages contain expectations and mandatory advertising language. These modalities are not interchangeable.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
          "quote": "distributors should not offer any gifts"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u9.1940",
          "quote": "It is an offence under section 103 of the SFO"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u20.5257",
          "quote": "they must comply with paragraph 2.3 of the Code of Conduct."
        }
      ]
    },
    "time": {
      "interpretation": "The only explicit calendar date identifies issuance of a referenced FAQ: 2010-09-30. It is not stated to be the effective date of the selected restriction. The circular's date, applicable version and any transition provisions are absent, so the formula contains no invented date condition.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u29.8110",
          "quote": "issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u30.8235",
          "quote": "from time to time."
        }
      ]
    },
    "dependencies": {
      "interpretation": "Although the packet's dependency list is empty, its text references external law, the Code, a FAQ, offering-document principles and advertising guidance. The supplied quotations support this proposal, but the missing materials prevent a complete assessment of definitions, exceptions, versions and related duties. Paragraph 9's gift-classification qualification remains relevant to paragraph 10; section 103 is a separate path.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u12.2646",
          "quote": "Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u14.3675",
          "quote": "in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u29.8110",
          "quote": "The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "unit_accounting": [
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u0.2",
      "quote": "Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)",
      "treatment": "Defines the circular's actor scope and establishes the fund-promotion context."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u1.497",
      "quote": "Background",
      "treatment": "Heading; creates no independent condition."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u2.512",
      "quote": "beyond the product features set out in the funds’ offering documents.",
      "treatment": "Distinguishes distributor-added features from documented fund features; does not classify every addition as a gift."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u3.792",
      "quote": "albeit without any guaranteed or specific rates.",
      "treatment": "Describes a separate service arrangement later addressed by advertising provisions."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u4.1115",
      "quote": "aggressive and high-profile marketing campaigns.",
      "treatment": "Observational context; aggressiveness is not made a prerequisite of the gift restriction."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u5.1267",
      "quote": "Guaranteed returns",
      "treatment": "Heading introducing the relevant return arrangements."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u6.1287",
      "quote": "Section 103 of the Securities and Futures Ordinance (Cap. 571) (SFO)",
      "treatment": "Identifies the separate statutory dependency."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u7.1360",
      "quote": "the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return)",
      "treatment": "Separates fund return from the distributor top-up; neither component is automatically a gift."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u8.1651",
      "quote": "if the return to investors is determined by reference to the change in value of any securities (including funds).",
      "treatment": "Supplies a qualified structured-product classification condition, outside the selected formula."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u9.1940",
      "quote": "unless the SFC has authorised the issue or an exemption applies.",
      "treatment": "Records section 103's separate exception attachment; does not supply a gift exception."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u10.2239",
      "quote": "may create a misleading impression that these returns are provided by the underlying fund(s).",
      "treatment": "Explains a distinct disclosure and misleading-impression concern."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u11.2603",
      "quote": "Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct",
      "treatment": "Identifies the selected restriction's Code dependency."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u12.2646",
      "quote": "as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.",
      "treatment": "Preserves the qualified classification of returns and incentives and the independent relevance of the gift restriction."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u13.2987",
      "quote": "The purpose of the requirement is to avoid the use of gifts to distract investors from the features and risks of a particular product.",
      "treatment": "Primary rule, discount exception and product-type extension. Purpose explains the rule; actual demonstrated distraction is not stated as an additional prerequisite."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u14.3675",
      "quote": "in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.",
      "treatment": "Connects the separate restrictions; does not impose an unconditional ban on every additional return or incentive."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u15.4022",
      "quote": "Lock-up period and dealing frequency",
      "treatment": "Heading marking a separate subject."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u16.4063",
      "quote": "even though the fund provided daily dealing arrangements.",
      "treatment": "Describes distributor restrictions inconsistent with underlying dealing arrangements; outside the gift control."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u17.4359",
      "quote": "They should not restrict a client’s right to redeem his or her investment in a fund pursuant to the dealing frequency specified in the fund’s offering documents.",
      "treatment": "Separate redemption-right restriction and fairness dependency."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u18.4879",
      "quote": "use their best endeavours to adhere to a fund’s dealing frequency",
      "treatment": "Separate dealing expectation; administrative procedures are not a gift-rule exception."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u19.5230",
      "quote": "Other marketing issues",
      "treatment": "Heading marking additional marketing controls."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u20.5257",
      "quote": "they do not contain any misleading or deceptive information",
      "treatment": "Separate advertising requirement for services, including those without guaranteed returns."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u21.5903",
      "quote": "consistent with the principles under the SFC’s Advertising Guidelines Applicable to Collective Investment Schemes Authorized under the Product Codes",
      "treatment": "External advertising-guidance dependency; not encoded as a gift condition."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u22.6374",
      "quote": "the advertisements should not draw a parallel between the services and the placement of cash on deposits",
      "treatment": "Separate restriction on misleading return and deposit comparisons; no gift exception follows."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u23.7007",
      "quote": "may take regulatory action and issue further guidance where appropriate.",
      "treatment": "States possible regulatory action and future guidance, not a fact establishing a violation or a commencement date."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u24.7186",
      "quote": "Intermediaries Supervision Department",
      "treatment": "Institutional attribution; no independent operative condition."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u25.7275",
      "quote": "Intermediaries Division",
      "treatment": "Institutional attribution; no independent operative condition."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u26.7393",
      "quote": "Securities and Futures Commission",
      "treatment": "Institutional attribution; does not independently verify authority or currency."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u27.7511",
      "quote": "all key features and risks of the fund shall be highlighted prominently in a succinct manner for investors.",
      "treatment": "Footnote supporting offering-document disclosure obligations, separate from the selected gift restriction."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u28.7987",
      "quote": "The Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission",
      "treatment": "Expands the Code's title; does not establish any selected actor's licensing or registration status."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u29.8110",
      "quote": "issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.",
      "treatment": "Identifies the dated FAQ supporting the product-type discussion; its full answer is absent."
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "db43e253bea18.u30.8235",
      "quote": "As supplemented by the frequently asked questions and other guidance issued by the SFC from time to time.",
      "treatment": "Qualifies the advertising-guidance dependency, without supplying the supplements or a fixed applicable version."
    }
  ]
}"}}
